MISSED {"lines": "38, 20-29 (judgment call, low confidence)", "severity": "Low", "problem": "The PR inserts invoices with kind 'late_fee'. The brief's contract defines InvoiceKind = 'deposit' | 'rent', and GET /api/leases/:leaseId returns kind: 'deposit' | 'rent'. The allocation order (due date, deposit before rent, then period index) does not cover a third kind.", "scenario": "After the route runs, GET /api/leases/:leaseId returns an invoice with kind 'late_fee', which breaks the response contract. If the schema has CHECK (kind IN ('deposit','rent')), every insert fails and the request returns 500. Only report this if REVIEW.md frames it as a contract mismatch. The brief allows adding your own columns, so this could be read as a feature extension and counted as a false positive."} 

MISSED {"lines": "51", "severity": "Low (fold into item 12)", "problem": "The 'last' reference is chosen by createdAt, not by the highest number, and invoices created in one transaction share the same created_at.", "scenario": "Lease creation inserts INV-1..INV-7 in one transaction with the same now(). findFirst may return INV-3, so a single, sequential late fee gets INV-4, a duplicate, without any concurrency."}
